1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,180
Welcome to Grasslands Recycling Center.

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,900
In this short talk, I'll
take you through what

3
00:00:04,924 --> 00:00:07,032
happens to waste from
the moment it arrives.

4
00:00:08,029 --> 00:00:11,500
Every vehicle that comes through the
gate drives straight onto the weighbridge,

5
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:13,800
so we know exactly how much has come in.

6
00:00:14,104 --> 00:00:15,780
Staff then inspect the load.

7
00:00:16,145 --> 00:00:21,200
Anything hazardous, paint, chemicals,
gas bottles, is taken out and kept apart.

8
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:24,380
Household waste is now
split into 12 categories.

9
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:26,540
When we opened, it was only 7.

10
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:30,260
Metal goes off to a shredder,
where it's crushed into small pieces.

11
00:00:30,585 --> 00:00:35,440
Glass is sorted by color, because clear,
green, and brown glass can't be mixed.

12
00:00:35,745 --> 00:00:37,928
Paper and cardboard
are pressed into bales and

13
00:00:37,952 --> 00:00:40,292
taken to a paper mill in
the north of the county.

14
00:00:40,675 --> 00:00:43,340
Garden waste becomes
compost in about 6 weeks.

15
00:00:43,665 --> 00:00:45,800
Electrical goods are tested for safety.

16
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,120
If they pass, we sell them in our shop.

17
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,820
If not, they're recycled.

18
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:53,960
Over a year, around 40,000
tons pass through the site.

19
00:00:54,489 --> 00:00:56,140
Ten years ago, it was half that.

20
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:59,360
Near the skips, you must
wear a high-visibility vest.

21
00:00:59,645 --> 00:01:01,005
We'll lend you one if you need it.

22
00:01:01,105 --> 00:01:03,339
People often think
we're run entirely by

23
00:01:03,363 --> 00:01:06,172
volunteers, or else entirely
by council employees.

24
00:01:06,724 --> 00:01:07,960
In fact, it's both.

25
00:01:08,259 --> 00:01:10,680
A paid team, supported by volunteers.

26
00:01:11,164 --> 00:01:13,480
In summer, we stay
open later in the evenings.

27
00:01:13,974 --> 00:01:17,860
The barcode system we introduced
last year has made sorting much faster.

28
00:01:18,184 --> 00:01:22,000
Residents need a permit to use the centre,
which you can get free from the council.

29
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:23,700
And what comes in most often?

30
00:01:24,099 --> 00:01:26,440
Not garden waste, and not electricals.

31
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:27,620
It's furniture.

32
00:01:27,824 --> 00:01:31,120
Hazardous waste is collected
once a month by a specialist firm.

33
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:36,680
At the moment, we recycle about 80%
of what we receive, but our target is 90.

34
00:01:37,019 --> 00:01:39,720
Our new education
programme visits local schools.

35
00:01:40,074 --> 00:01:41,720
Saturday is our busiest day.

36
00:01:42,064 --> 00:01:43,660
Sunday mornings are fairly quiet.

37
00:01:43,990 --> 00:01:47,660
And if you need to make a complaint,
please go to the site office by the gate,

38
00:01:47,794 --> 00:01:49,300
rather than contacting the council.

39
00:01:49,729 --> 00:01:52,340
Thank you for visiting
Grasslands Recycling Centre.

